WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.709 --> 00:00:03.212
So, you've made it
to the end of Squid Game,

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:04.963
you've survived
all six games,

00:00:05.047 --> 00:00:06.840
you've gasped
through the twists and turns

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:09.468
and cried a small
ocean's worth of tears

00:00:09.551 --> 00:00:11.929
watching two friends
play a game of marbles.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:15.807
We made a pinkie promise
to be each other's gganbu.

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:17.726
If you know, you know.

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:19.061
And now
you're looking for more:

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:20.771
more thrillers
that pitch players

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.272
in battles to the death,

00:00:22.356 --> 00:00:24.858
more dramas
about desperate struggles,

00:00:24.942 --> 00:00:27.361
or maybe just more film
and TV from Korea.

00:00:27.444 --> 00:00:29.863
Whatever your wants,
Netflix has you covered.

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:37.204
If Squid Game has you hooked
on sinister games

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:39.873
then Alice in Borderland
will scratch that itch.

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:41.625
In this hit
Japanese thriller,

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.169
Tokyo is transformed
into a ghost town

00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:47.047
as three heroes are pulled
into a violent game show

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.508
where they complete tasks
to earn more time

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:50.884
to explore
and escape the city.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.427
And if time runs out…

00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:56.306
Let's just say,
don't let time run out.

00:00:57.182 --> 00:00:58.934
Based on the Haro Aso manga,

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:02.187
Alice in Borderland shares
Squid Game's sense of style,

00:01:02.271 --> 00:01:04.356
and offers deadly takes
on playground favourites

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.275
like Tag or Hide and Seek.

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:08.360
Can gaming-obsessed
slacker Ryohei Arisu

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:10.779
get his friends safely
through the challenges?

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:13.240
Find out only on Netflix.

00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:19.746
Brazilian thriller
3% may unfold

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.748
on the other side
of the Earth to Squid Game,

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:23.458
but it offers
an equally thrilling take

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:25.460
on life-or-death
competition.

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:27.087
In a bleak future society,

00:01:27.171 --> 00:01:28.964
citizens are trapped
in poverty

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:30.424
unless they win a place

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:31.925
in an affluent
island paradise.

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:34.386
When residents
hit 20 years of age,

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:36.013
they take part
in "The Process,"

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.015
a series of tests designed

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.058
to whittle the group down
to the three percent

00:01:40.142 --> 00:01:42.644
who get a ticket
to the chosen land.

00:01:42.728 --> 00:01:44.479
It's a complex look
at the inequality

00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:46.315
that drives
violent competition

00:01:46.398 --> 00:01:47.441
between good people,

00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:49.526
while also delivering
tense thrills

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.653
as the cast tackle
the challenges.

00:01:51.737 --> 00:01:54.406
Over 33 episodes,
a fitting number,

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:57.367
3% will get under your skin
and stay there.

00:02:00.245 --> 00:02:02.998
Like Squid Game, Sweet Home
hails from South Korea,

00:02:03.081 --> 00:02:06.251
but this gruesome horror has
a slightly different energy.

00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:07.961
Fragile teen Cha Hyun Soo

00:02:08.045 --> 00:02:10.339
moves into a dilapidated
apartment block

00:02:10.422 --> 00:02:12.007
to escape a family tragedy

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.468
and is met
by unsympathetic neighbours.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:15.969
Don't die here.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:20.557
You'll just cause trouble
for a lot of people here.

00:02:20.641 --> 00:02:22.392
Won't be bothering her
for a cup of sugar.

00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:24.895
But grumpy residents are
the least of his worries.

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:26.522
The security guard's
in a trance,

00:02:26.605 --> 00:02:28.607
there are bloody trails
in the corridors

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.276
and nosebleeds breaking out
across the building.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.654
Oh, and an army of demons
banging on the front door.

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:38.242
Watching its cast
come together

00:02:38.325 --> 00:02:40.827
to fight the apocalypse
will warm your heart,

00:02:40.911 --> 00:02:43.121
when the monsters aren't
trying to eat it, of course.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.087
Where Squid Game
has a pig full of money,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.798
Okja is about a pig
worth a lot of money.

00:02:52.881 --> 00:02:53.799
Meet Okja,

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:55.592
a genetically-modified
super-hog

00:02:55.676 --> 00:02:56.760
bred by Tilda Swinton

00:02:56.844 --> 00:02:59.221
as part of her plan
to bring home the bacon

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:00.889
in more ways than one.

00:03:00.973 --> 00:03:03.016
Raised by a girl
in South Korea,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.185
Okja grows big enough
to draw the attention

00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:07.229
of her corporate creators.

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:08.480
Enter Jake Gyllenhaal,

00:03:08.564 --> 00:03:11.024
in one of his wildest
performances to date…

00:03:11.108 --> 00:03:13.944
Dr Johnny's…

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:17.656
Magical Animals!

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:20.450
…as he takes the plus-sized
porker to New York,

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.787
setting the little girl on a
quest to save her piggy pal.

00:03:23.871 --> 00:03:25.539
From the mind
of Bong Joon-ho,

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:26.832
the director of Parasite,

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:28.292
the first
foreign-language film

00:03:28.375 --> 00:03:30.294
to win Best Picture
at the Oscars,

00:03:30.377 --> 00:03:32.754
Okja is a romp
full of laughs, shocks,

00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:35.424
and many shots of Gyllenhaal
in terrible shorts.

00:03:36.008 --> 00:03:40.971
Are you ready?

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.639
Yes, we are, Jake.

00:03:44.016 --> 00:03:44.850
Like Squid Game,

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.393
Extracurricular
is another show

00:03:46.476 --> 00:03:47.728
looking at
the extreme lengths

00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.521
people will go to
for a paycheque.

00:03:49.605 --> 00:03:52.733
Oh Ji-soo is a brainy
but bashful student.

00:03:52.816 --> 00:03:54.026
Think straight A grades

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:56.820
and a crush on a girl
with slow-motion hair.

00:03:56.904 --> 00:03:58.405
But he lives a double life,

00:03:58.488 --> 00:04:01.617
running security service
for illegal female escorts.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.785
Operating as
the mysterious "Uncle,"

00:04:03.869 --> 00:04:05.913
he protects the girls
from violent clients

00:04:05.996 --> 00:04:07.748
and takes a cut
of their earnings.

00:04:07.831 --> 00:04:10.584
But when his crush takes an
interest in his side hustle,

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:11.752
can Ji-soo balance

00:04:11.835 --> 00:04:14.505
his high-stakes business
with his student life?

00:04:14.588 --> 00:04:16.548
Extracurricular
is like Breaking Bad

00:04:16.632 --> 00:04:17.549
for the sex trade,

00:04:17.633 --> 00:04:19.885
minus the hazmat suits,
obviously.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.762
You'll be hooked
after just one episode.

00:04:23.555 --> 00:04:26.266
Psychokinesis is a superhero
film with a twist.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.977
When a crooked security
guard drinks infected water,

00:04:29.061 --> 00:04:30.604
he gains superpowers,

00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:32.814
but can he be bothered
to use them for good?

00:04:32.898 --> 00:04:35.442
Great power comes
with little responsibility.

00:04:35.526 --> 00:04:37.861
Well, until bullying
businessmen come

00:04:37.945 --> 00:04:40.072
for his estranged daughter's
fried chicken shop.

00:04:40.155 --> 00:04:42.574
Time for some
finger-licking justice.

00:04:42.658 --> 00:04:44.576
From the director
of Train to Busan,

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:46.078
Psychokinesis delivers all

00:04:46.161 --> 00:04:48.247
the wham-bam action
of a comic book romp,

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.166
but with a nod to Korea's
struggling underdogs.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.335
If you enjoyed
Gi-Hun's Squid Game journey

00:04:53.418 --> 00:04:55.170
from selfish gambler
to do-gooder,

00:04:55.254 --> 00:04:56.839
then Psychokinesis
is another one

00:04:56.922 --> 00:04:58.257
to add to your watchlist.

00:05:02.886 --> 00:05:04.596
The Uncanny Counter
shares Squid Game's

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.265
love of a red tracksuit,

00:05:06.348 --> 00:05:08.976
although, here, the outfits
are worn by the good guys,

00:05:09.059 --> 00:05:10.853
a team of superpowered
Counters

00:05:10.936 --> 00:05:12.646
who protect the Earth
from evil souls

00:05:12.729 --> 00:05:14.147
escaping from the afterlife.

00:05:14.231 --> 00:05:15.732
When they aren't
thrashing demons,

00:05:15.816 --> 00:05:17.609
the Counters
hide their identity

00:05:17.693 --> 00:05:19.236
by running
a noodle restaurant.

00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:23.240
So, do not forget
to tip your waiter.

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:24.867
Into their world
wanders So Mun,

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.785
who becomes the unlikely
host of the soul

00:05:26.869 --> 00:05:28.328
of a recently killed
Counter.

00:05:31.373 --> 00:05:33.792
Can So Mun win over
his fellow heroes?

00:05:33.876 --> 00:05:36.086
Will demonic forces
conquer the Earth?

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.880
And how is he going
to get that birthday cake

00:05:37.963 --> 00:05:39.298
out of his hair?

00:05:39.381 --> 00:05:41.008
Expect answers
to all this and more

00:05:41.091 --> 00:05:42.426
in The Uncanny Counter.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.807
Time to Hunt
is an action-packed thriller

00:05:48.891 --> 00:05:50.475
starring Squid Game's
Park Hae Soo

00:05:50.559 --> 00:05:52.060
as a cold-blooded killer.

00:05:52.144 --> 00:05:54.730
Having wowed us as
Choo Sang-Woo in Squid Game,

00:05:54.813 --> 00:05:57.191
he plays a very different
kind of bad guy here,

00:05:57.274 --> 00:05:59.943
a professional hit man hired
to hunt down three friends

00:06:00.027 --> 00:06:01.695
who robbed
from the wrong casino.

00:06:01.778 --> 00:06:04.907
Wave goodbye to Squid Game's
sly, white-collar criminal

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:06.992
and say hello
to a human terminator

00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:09.328
who could give John Wick
a run for his money.

00:06:10.704 --> 00:06:12.080
We knew he was bad news

00:06:12.164 --> 00:06:13.999
the moment we saw
his ear collection.

00:06:14.082 --> 00:06:15.292
Never a good sign, is it?

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:16.543
The way Time to Hunt

00:06:16.627 --> 00:06:18.587
flips from heist thriller
to chase film

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:19.963
makes it a brilliantly
tense way

00:06:20.047 --> 00:06:21.882
to spend a couple of hours.

00:06:28.972 --> 00:06:31.433
Interested in checking out
more Korean cinema,

00:06:31.517 --> 00:06:33.143
then why not try
The Drug King?

00:06:33.227 --> 00:06:34.853
Set in the 1970s,

00:06:34.937 --> 00:06:36.647
it tells the true story
of Lee Doo-sam,

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.690
a drug smuggler
who climbs the ranks

00:06:38.774 --> 00:06:39.858
of the criminal underworld.

00:06:39.942 --> 00:06:41.443
Think of it
as a Korean Scarface,

00:06:41.527 --> 00:06:44.029
only with lovable superstar
Song Kang-ho

00:06:44.112 --> 00:06:46.281
instead of shouty Al Pacino.

00:06:46.365 --> 00:06:48.909
Song's natural charisma
is put to excellent use

00:06:48.992 --> 00:06:50.369
as Doo-sam charms his way

00:06:50.452 --> 00:06:52.329
across international
borders.

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:54.706
He even convinces
his very own Walter White

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:56.041
to work in a pig farm.

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:57.084
Good people skills.

00:06:57.167 --> 00:06:59.419
Of course, if you've seen
any gangster epic,

00:06:59.503 --> 00:07:02.130
you'll know that what goes
up must come down.

00:07:02.214 --> 00:07:03.382
As police close in

00:07:03.465 --> 00:07:05.467
and Doo-sam gets hooked
on his own product,

00:07:05.551 --> 00:07:07.302
can he escape the chaos?

00:07:07.386 --> 00:07:09.054
Check out
The Drug King to find out.

00:07:13.517 --> 00:07:15.811
If you thought the players
in Squid Game had it bad,

00:07:15.894 --> 00:07:17.771
wait until you meet
the unlucky contestants

00:07:17.855 --> 00:07:19.147
in The Platform.

00:07:19.231 --> 00:07:21.191
In this Netflix
Original movie,

00:07:21.275 --> 00:07:22.734
people live
in a towering structure

00:07:22.818 --> 00:07:24.152
where food
is transported down

00:07:24.236 --> 00:07:25.779
from the top to the bottom.

00:07:25.863 --> 00:07:26.697
The catch?

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.157
It's one meal to feed
the entire lot of them.

00:07:29.241 --> 00:07:31.201
So the more that people eat
on the levels above,

00:07:31.285 --> 00:07:33.912
the less there is
for the people below.

00:07:33.996 --> 00:07:36.290
And there are
many people below.

00:07:36.373 --> 00:07:39.293
To give any more away about
this dystopian sci-fi horror

00:07:39.376 --> 00:07:42.546
would spoil one of 2020's
most devious thrillers.

00:07:42.629 --> 00:07:44.047
You'll never look
at leftover food

00:07:44.131 --> 00:07:45.340
the same way again,

00:07:45.424 --> 00:07:47.634
so probably not one
to watch during dinner.

00:07:50.304 --> 00:07:51.597
If you like Squid Game,

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.057
those are just a few of the
incredible shows and films

00:07:54.141 --> 00:07:56.852
available on Netflix
that we'd suggest watching.

00:07:56.935 --> 00:07:58.353
We'd love to hear
your recommendations

00:07:58.437 --> 00:07:59.354
in the comments.

00:07:59.438 --> 00:08:01.273
And make sure
to give this video a like

00:08:01.356 --> 00:08:02.566
if you find it helpful,

00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:04.234
and click
that notification bell

00:08:04.318 --> 00:08:06.361
so we can be
gganbu for life.

